// A placeholder marks a position the caller fills before the query runs. Unbound, it used to be
// rejected for the wrong reason: the comparison template found no right operand and reported
// "template {0} > {1} references argument {1} but only 1 were provided" -- an internal message
// about a SQL template, not about the query. Now the placeholder itself is reported, on the #x.
FIND orders o
FILTER o.freight > #x
FETCH o.order_id
